&gt;&gt;&gt; Optimal	Production
&gt;&gt; Suitable	Hospitals, Durability
X Inadvisable 	Bedding

Polyester is synthetic fabric made from polymer fibers. It's exceptionally easy to work with making it a commodity material, insulates well, but isn't the most comfortable in hot climates. It's antimicrobial properties make it an excellent candidate for hospital bedding.</description>
